# proto-file: proto/stipulator/v1/policy.proto
# proto-message: stipulator.v1.TestPolicy

invocations {
  name: "race"
  timeout {
    seconds: 7200
  }
  go {
    packages: "./..."
    race: true
    # 60m governs the per-binary cap of the WITNESS run, which stipulator
    # executes width-capped (2 on this 24-core host). Evidence, 2026-08-28,
    # idle machine: the race detector measures 4.06x on the analysis-heavy
    # observability proofs (TestReadOnlyObservabilityProof 3m42s plain vs
    # 15m02s race, unconstrained); the plain closure package is 544s
    # (CI-measured 2026-08-27); the fleet sweep observed 18m elapsed at the
    # old 30m cap's kill inside that one test under the witness env (a
    # lower bound on the unit). Baseline under THIS cap: the first check
    # re-executed 502 witnesses — the whole 196-witness closure unit
    # included — in 35m58s end-to-end wall (bracketed 2026-08-28
    # 13:13:10-13:49:08 local), an upper bound on the closure unit, so it
    # sits well inside 60m. A budget overrun here is a real finding:
    # re-measure the witness-width-capped unit before raising the number.
    # The plain-suite budget for the same packages lives in
    # .github/workflows/ci.yaml with its own measured curve — when the
    # closure proofs grow, re-measure both. The 7200s invocation budget
    # above bounds the whole run.
    args: "-test.timeout=60m"
    bracket_paths: "/bin/sh"
    bracket_paths: "/usr/bin/sh"
    bracket_paths: "/usr/bin/git"
    bracket_paths: "/usr/bin/taskset"
    bracket_paths: "go.work"
    bracket_paths: "go.mod"
    bracket_paths: "go.sum"
    bracket_paths: "guard"
    bracket_paths: "runtimeinput"
    bracket_paths: "closure"
    bracket_paths: "internal"
    assume_pure: true
  }
}
